      "notes": [
        "All 5 patch functions are implemented and verified. The DOM anchors (data-wp-id on rows, id=project-status-badge, id=synthesis-link-row, id=health-badge, id=timing-info and child spans) are all in place in renderProjectDetail. QA should verify: (1) patch functions are no-ops when elements are absent, (2) _patchWpRow leaves WP ID and assigned-to cells untouched, (3) _patchSynthesisLink correctly toggles display:none, (4) _patchHealthBadge mirrors the initial render logic exactly, (5) no raw badge spans are used in the new code."
      ]
    },
    {
      "from_agent": "QA",
      "to_agent": "Reviewer",
      "timestamp": "2026-06-09T16:55:37Z",
      "notes": [
        "All 6 ACs verified PASS. Patch functions are correctly scoped, use statusBadge() for badge rendering, perform fresh DOM queries, apply compare-and-swap guards, and contain zero raw badge spans. 1229/1229 GUI regression tests pass. Code is clean and ready for code-review. Note for Reviewer: (1) _patchHealthBadge logic mirrors the inline health badge code in renderProjectDetail lines 758-771 — duplication is intentional for now per Developer note, but worth flagging as a consolidation opportunity. (2) _patchSynthesisLink injection fallback (querySelector('.card-title')) is dead code since synthesis-link-row is always pre-rendered; low risk but could be simplified."
